# ==============================================================================
# .gitattributes (repository root)
# ==============================================================================
#
# The native libraries and the two licence texts beside each of them, under
# src/CodeBrix.Audio.Vorbis/runtimes/<rid>/native/, are packed into the NuGet
# package exactly as they are on disk. They must be byte-identical on every
# runtime identifier and on every checkout, whichever operating system did the
# checkout and whichever one runs `dotnet pack`. With core.autocrlf=true (the
# Git for Windows default) and no rule here, a Windows checkout rewrote the
# LICENSE-Vorbis.txt / LICENSE-Ogg.txt copies with CRLF line endings, so a
# package built on Windows shipped different licence bytes for the Linux and
# Android RIDs than one built on Linux. -text switches every conversion off.
#
# vorbis-native-tools/.gitattributes protects the SOURCES of those texts
# (licenses/LICENSE-Vorbis.txt, ogg/COPYING, vorbis/COPYING) the same way; this
# rule protects the adopted copies that ship.
#
# The binaries are marked explicitly too, so no diff or merge driver ever
# treats them as text.
# ==============================================================================

src/CodeBrix.Audio.Vorbis/runtimes/**                       -text
src/CodeBrix.Audio.Vorbis/runtimes/**/*.dll                 binary
src/CodeBrix.Audio.Vorbis/runtimes/**/*.so                  binary
src/CodeBrix.Audio.Vorbis/runtimes/**/*.dylib               binary

# The committed pre-strip twins (vorbis-native-tools/unstripped/<rid>/).
vorbis-native-tools/unstripped/**/*.so                      binary
vorbis-native-tools/unstripped/**/*.dylib                   binary
vorbis-native-tools/unstripped/**/*.pdb                     binary
